seg-4bca83197ed6 = The default Cowell force model carries only the zonal field: the high-degree EGM2008 (Earth Gravitational Model { "2008" }) <b>tesseral</b> field (<c1/>, degree/order { "70" }, with a <c2/> loader for ICGEM (International Centre for Global Earth Models) files) is composed only into the precise ephemeris-fitting engine (<c3/>; see <a1><c4/></a1>); drag density is the <b>static</b> Vallado piecewise-exponential (solar-activity-independent), <b>not</b> NRLMSISE-00 (the Naval Research Laboratory Mass Spectrometer and Incoherent Scatter Radar Extended atmosphere model; the < { "5" } % thermospheric-density clause); SRP is the <b>cannonball</b> model with a geometric <b>conical umbra+penumbra</b> shadow (no solar limb darkening, no oblate-Earth shadow, no satellite shape/attitude); relativity covers the <b>Schwarzschild and Lense–Thirring</b> (frame-dragging) terms, both opt-in, but no PPN-parameter (PPN: parametrised post-Newtonian) tuning; <b>third-body/SRP use the low-precision ephemerides (~{ "0.005" }° Sun, ~{ "0.3" }° Moon), not DE/SPK-kernel accuracy</b>. The conservative force-model tiers (two-body → J2–J6 → Sun/Moon → SRP) are <b>VALIDATED against Orekit { "12.2" }</b> (worst { "0.08" } m over { "24" } h, <c5/>), and batch/sequential orbit determination is <b>VALIDATED against Orekit { "12.2" }</b>'s estimators (<c6/>); the drag tier and the absolute ephemeris/density input fidelity stay MODELLED; there is no GMAT (General Mission Analysis Tool) cross-check

