seg-f744a0c03b2c = FutureNAV optimism-gap study additions (modelled, internally cross-checked against closed forms — <b>not</b> externally validated, <b>not</b> a sim-to-field claim): a controlled <b>synthetic</b> study of the in-distribution→out-of-distribution AUC <b>optimism gap</b> for RF-impairment detectors. ({ "1" }) <b>Learned detectors</b> <c1/> — a fixed feature map + train-fit standardiser, a logistic-regression baseline (deterministic full-batch gradient descent), and a one-hidden-layer <b>MLP</b> (multilayer perceptron; seeded backprop SGD (stochastic gradient descent)) behind the same <c2/> trait the published-method baselines use. ({ "2" }) <b>Hand-derived statistics</b> <c3/> — percentile-bootstrap confidence intervals (CIs), <b>DeLong</b> AUC variance/CI, <b>Spearman</b> ρ, and <b>ridge</b> regression, each checked against a closed form (binormal AUC Φ(d′/√{ "2" }), a hand-worked DeLong variance, a textbook tied-rank ρ, exact OLS (ordinary least squares) recovery). ({ "3" }) <b>The study</b> <c4/> — per-class AUC, the per-<c5/> scaling-law trend (gap vs { "1" }−severity), and an <b>ID-only ridge gap predictor</b> that estimates the optimism gap from in-distribution diagnostics alone, scored <b>leave-one-detector-out</b> and <b>leave-one-class-out</b> against a predict-the-mean baseline. One-command artifact via <c6/>. Every number is an AUC over model-derived labels on a synthetic, parameter-grounded corpus; the gap is a synthetic→synthetic severity shift, never a field-detection result. Mapped into the machine-checked verification matrix (<c7/>, Validated⇒ExternalDataset invariant intact).

